'''2†.''' A painful swelling or sore under or about the toe- or finger-nails; a whitlow.
{{smaller block|Good to be layde unto . . . ulcered nayles or ''agnayles'', whiche is a paynefull swelling aboute the ioyntes and nayles.{{right|''Lyte'', Dodoens (1578), p. 258. (''N. E. D.'')}}
''Agnail'', a sore at the root of the nail on the fingers or toes.{{right|''Bailey'' (1721).}}}}
'''3.''' A hangnail; a small piece of partly separated skin at the root of a nail or beside it.

